      "locked": false,
      "text": "JavaScript:-\n\nVariable: A value that can be changed after it is assigned.\n👉 Example: age = 20 → later age = 21\nConstant: A value that cannot be changed after it is assigned.\n👉 Example: PI = 3.14\nlet: let is used to declare a variable whose value can be changed later.\n👉 Example: let age = 20; age = 21;\n\n\nDataTypes:\n* Javascript is dynamically typed language\n// Primitive\n// 7 types : String, Number, Boolean, null, undefined, Symbol, BigInt\n\nconst score = 100\nconst scoreVaule = 100.3\n\nconst isLoggedIn = false\nconst outsideTemp = null\nlet userEmail;\n\nconst id = Symbol('123')\nconsole.log(id === anotherId);\n\nconst bigNumber = 34545345253452345553n; \n\n\n\n// Non-Primitive (Reference)\n// Arrays, Objects, Functions\n\n\nconst heroes = [\"shaktiman\", \"naagraj\", \"doga\"]\nlet myObj = {\nname:\"Dhruv\",\nage:23,\n}\n\nconst myFunction = function(){\nconsole.log(\"Hello world\");\n}\n\nconsole.log(typeof bigNumber);\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "JavaScript:-\n\nVariable: A value that can be changed after it is assigned.\n👉 Example: age = 20 → later age = 21\nConstant: A value that cannot be changed after it is assigned.\n👉 Example: PI = 3.14\nlet: let is used to declare a variable whose value can be changed later.\n👉 Example: let age = 20; age = 21;\n\n\nDataTypes:\n* Javascript is dynamically typed language\n// Primitive\n// 7 types : String, Number, Boolean, null, undefined, Symbol, BigInt\n\nconst score = 100\nconst scoreVaule = 100.3\n\nconst isLoggedIn = false\nconst outsideTemp = null\nlet userEmail;\n\nconst id = Symbol('123')\nconsole.log(id === anotherId);\n\nconst bigNumber = 34545345253452345553n; \n\n\n\n// Non-Primitive (Reference)\n// Arrays, Objects, Functions\n\n\nconst heroes = [\"shaktiman\", \"naagraj\", \"doga\"]\nlet myObj = {\nname:\"Dhruv\",\nage:23,\n}\n\nconst myFunction = function(){\nconsole.log(\"Hello world\");\n}\n\nconsole.log(typeof bigNumber);\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
